<article class="env-lemma" id="066L">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/066L">Lemma <span data-tag="066L">15.68.13</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a ring map. Let $a, b \in \mathbf{Z}$. Let $K^\bullet $ be a complex of $A$-modules with tor amplitude in $[a, b]$. Then $K^\bullet \otimes _ A^{\mathbf{L}} B$ as a complex of $B$-modules has tor amplitude in $[a, b]$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0654" data-tag="0654">15.68.3</a> we can find a quasi-isomorphism $E^\bullet \to K^\bullet $ where $E^\bullet $ is a complex of flat $A$-modules with $E^ i = 0$ for $i \not\in [a, b]$. Then $E^\bullet \otimes _ A B$ computes $K^\bullet \otimes _ A ^{\mathbf{L}} B$ by construction and each $E^ i \otimes _ A B$ is a flat $B$-module by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00HI" data-tag="00HI">10.39.7</a>. Hence we conclude by Lemma <a href="/tag/0654" data-tag="0654">15.68.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>